              "cites": ["src:12"]
            }
          ],
          "costs_them": "He is either maintaining a parallel version-control habit to get a signal the tool does not give him, or paying the tax of asking a person every time it matters.",
          "fears": "That he acts on something that stopped being true months ago and nothing in the page warned him.",
          "dream_outcome": "The page tells him, at the top, when a human last confirmed it was still right, and tells its owner when that is overdue."
        }
      },
      "segments": ["seg:startup", "seg:enterprise"],
      "feature_ref": "feat:kb",
      "feature_note": "This is the clearest latent pain in the map and the most useful finding in it. redsparrow wishes for a freshness stamp and says he is sure it exists somewhere; Majestic121 replies in the same thread that it is a base feature of Notion, with recheck notifications on a 7, 30, 90 or custom day cycle. So the feature already ships and the buyer describing the pain did not know. That is a marketing gap rather than a product gap, and it is why this row is latent and revealed_by feat:kb rather than felt.",
      "cites": ["src:12", "src:20", "src:33"]
    }
